<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>KyAuth Flatpak repository</title>
<style>
  body { margin: 0 auto; max-width: 42rem; padding: 2rem 1.25rem; font: 16px/1.5 system-ui, sans-serif;
         color: #182326; background: #f8f6f0; }
  h1 { margin-top: 0; }
  pre { overflow-x: auto; padding: 1rem; border: 1px solid #e4dfd3; border-radius: 12px; background: #fff; }
  a { color: #a33614; }
  p.note { color: #566461; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>KyAuth for Nura and Linux desktops</h1>
<p>Authenticator codes and KyIdentity push sign-in approvals. This is KyAuth's signed Flatpak
repository: install from it once and <code>flatpak update</code> keeps KyAuth current.</p>
<pre>flatpak remote-add --if-not-exists flathub https://flathub.org/repo/flathub.flatpakrepo
flatpak remote-add --if-not-exists kyauth @PAGES_URL@/kyauth.flatpakrepo
flatpak install kyauth app.busnes.kyauth</pre>
<p class="note">Flathub provides the KDE runtime. Every commit here is signed, and the key is in
<a href="kyauth.flatpakrepo">kyauth.flatpakrepo</a>, so Flatpak refuses anything else.</p>
<p>Ubuntu Touch: download the <code>.click</code> from the
<a href="https://github.com/@REPOSITORY@/releases/latest">latest release</a>.</p>
</body>
</html>
